    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Variational methods are a popular paradigm to overcome the difficulties related to inverse imaging problems: they seek an estimate of the unknown image by minimizing a functional encoding information on the noise and prior beliefs on the image. For image denoising, denoting by y ∈ Rn the (vectorised) data corrupted by Additive White Gaussian Noise (AWGN), variational methods solve"
