    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "where x∗ depends on a certain number of parameters λ ∈ Λ possibly involved in the so-called regularisation term R. In general, flexible models are characterised by a large number of parameters for which robust selection strategies need to be introduced. How to properly select parameters in variational models is an issue that has attracted the interest of many researchers working on inverse problems."
